      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you double-check to see if only `elm` is failing as we discussed?\n\nI suspect not; IIRC, `elm` is usually the first board to be built.\n\nYou are adding `__ec_align4` to this struct, which looks like it\u0027s forcing 4 byte alignment that would apply to all boards (assuming `CONFIG_HOSTCMD_ALIGNED` is set). See [this comment](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/ec_commands.h;l\u003d615-641;drc\u003d269d738bf7a8fb02eec4479aa52ce92651e18f0e).\n\n(Separately, if you want to do some more cleanup, it looks like the [`todo` macros](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/ec_commands.h;l\u003d669-678;drc\u003d269d738bf7a8fb02eec4479aa52ce92651e18f0e) have been needing replacement for nine years. Now that we have `compare_builds` and `BULID_ASSERT`, we can verify that updating them does not change anything.)",
